{"slug": "tequila-watermelon-punch", "nyt_id": 12675, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/12675-tequila-watermelon-punch", "name": "Tequila-Watermelon Punch", "author": "Rosie Schaap", "description": "To make watermelon purée, put seedless chunks of watermelon in a blender and pulse, then push the purée through a mesh sieve to make it smoother. (Cutting a whole watermelon might make your kitchen look like a Gallagher set, so it’s O.K. to use precut watermelon from a supermarket.)", "servings": {"text": "", "min": null, "max": null, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": null, "raw": {}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "3 parts watermelon purée", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "parts watermelon purée", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 part silver tequila", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "part silver tequila", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "½ part fresh lime juice", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "part fresh lime juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "Seltzer", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "seltzer", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Sliced jalapeño", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "sliced jalapeño", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "Coarse sea salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "coarse sea salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "Ice", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "ice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Agave nectar (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "agave nectar", "preparation": null, "optional": true}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "In a large pitcher or bowl, stir together the watermelon purée, tequila and lime juice."}, {"position": 2, "text": "To sweeten, adjust with agave nectar."}, {"position": 3, "text": "To serve, pour into glasses over ice, top each glass with seltzer, a pinch of sea salt and slices of jalapeño."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 173.2, "protein_g": 3.5, "carbohydrates_g": 42.9, "fat_g": 0.9, "saturated_fat_g": 0.1, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 0.0, "sodium_mg": 1393.8, "fiber_g": 2.3, "sugar_g": 35.2, "unsaturated_fat_g": 0.5, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": [], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["cocktails", "lime", "not-shoppable-ic", "summer", "tequila", "watermelon", "punches"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/06/09/multimedia/09FD-tequilawatermelonpunch-1-vclp/09FD-tequilawatermelonpunch-1-vclp-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 399}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2012-08-08", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T03:15:44.016823+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "terrine-de-caneton-a-lancienne", "nyt_id": 1180, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1180-terrine-de-caneton-a-lancienne", "name": "Terrine de Caneton a l'Ancienne", "author": "Nancy Harmon Jenkins", "description": "“It is true, as has often been observed, that a terrine is nothing more than a meatloaf with a French accent,” wrote Nancy Harmon Jenkins in 1987, part of a piece that brought this recipe to The Times. Terrine isn’t a weeknight dish, but a true indulgence for a special occasion. Whether it’s for a holiday or a dinner party, terrine is, in fact, fortunately a lot like meatloaf: It improves with age, so it’s great the next day, tucked into a sandwich, or spread onto a baguette. Don’t forget the cornichons, or, as Ms. Harmon suggests, the bread-and-butter pickles. They’re a briny contrast to the terrine’s creaminess.", "servings": {"text": "10 to 12 servings", "min": 10, "max": 12, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 90, "cook_minutes": 150, "total_minutes": 240, "raw": {"total": "4 hours", "prep": "1 hour 30 minutes", "cook": "2 hours 30 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 (4 ½-pound) duckling", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "(4 ½-pound) duckling", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "8 ounces pork liver", "group": null, "quantity": 8.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "pork liver", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 medium carrot, scraped and coarsely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium carrot", "preparation": "scraped and coarsely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 medium turnip, peeled and coarsely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium turnip", "preparation": "peeled and coarsely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 medium onion, peeled and coarsely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium onion", "preparation": "peeled and coarsely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 medium tomato, coarsely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium tomato", "preparation": "coarsely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "2 cups water", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Herb bouquet (13 sprigs parsley, 2 sprigs thyme, 1 bay leaf and 1 leaf of fresh celery tied in cheesecloth)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "herb bouquet (13 sprigs parsley", "preparation": "2 sprigs thyme, 1 bay leaf and 1 leaf of fresh celery tied in cheesecloth)", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 ½ teaspoons salt, or to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 2.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": "or to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "10 or more dashes freshly ground black pepper, or to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 10.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "or more dashes freshly ground black pepper", "preparation": "or to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "4 eggs, lightly beaten", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "eggs", "preparation": "lightly beaten", "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "2 tablespoons heavy cream", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "heavy cream", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "2 garlic cloves, peeled and finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "garlic cloves", "preparation": "peeled and finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "4 shallots, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "shallots", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "1 tablespoon chopped parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "¼ teaspoon or more quatre epices, made from 10 ground cloves, 1 ground cinnamon stick, ⅔ teaspoon ground ginger and ¾ teaspoon freshly grated nutmeg", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "or more quatre epices", "preparation": "made from 10 ground cloves, 1 ground cinnamon stick, ⅔ teaspoon ground ginger and ¾ teaspoon freshly grated nutmeg", "optional": false}, {"position": 17, "raw": "1 teaspoon freshly ground white pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "freshly ground white pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 18, "raw": "¼ cup Armagnac (2 ounces)", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "armagnac (2 ounces)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 19, "raw": "4 ounces clarified butter or rendered chicken fat", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "clarified butter or rendered chicken fat", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Bone duck, or have butcher do it, scraping away meat and ligaments. Save bones, liver and skin. Discard sinews. In workbowl of a food processor fitted with a metal blade, puree all fat and a 4-by-5-inch piece of skin. Set aside."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Cut pork liver into small pieces. Process liver and duck meat briefly, using pulse button (you need not rinse bowl of food processor). Set aside."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Crack duck bones into small pieces and brown lightly in bits of duck fat in a medium-size skillet. Drain off any fat. Add carrot, turnip, onion, tomato, 2 cups water and the herb bouquet, bring to a boil and skim carefully. Lower heat and reduce liquid to 2 tablespoons of duck glaze; this will take about 45 minutes. Scrape glaze into a small bowl to cool. Discard solids in skillet."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Meanwhile, in a large bowl combine ground pork liver and duck meat, pureed skin and fat, 2 ½ teaspoons salt, freshly ground pepper, eggs, cream, garlic, shallots, parsley, quatre epices and freshly ground white pepper. Blend well."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Fold in reserved duck glaze. Pat mixture into a bowl and spread Armagnac on top. Let stand, uncovered, 2 to 3 hours at room temperature, or, covered, overnight in the refrigerator. (Mixture should come to room temperature before proceeding with next step.)"}, {"position": 6, "text": "Preheat oven to 300 degrees."}, {"position": 7, "text": "Stir mixture to loosen. Pack into a 1 ¾-quart terrine or loaf pan. Smooth it down, cover with foil and set in a larger pan of hot water. Place on oven's middle shelf and bake 1 ½ hours. Remove foil covering, lower oven temperature to 225 degrees and bake 1 hour longer."}, {"position": 8, "text": "Remove terrine from oven and let cool 30 minutes. Cover with foil, a dish or flat board and, on top of this, a weight (a 2- or 3-pound can will do). Let cool. When completely cold, refrigerate. Remove weight the following day. Cover with melted butter or chicken fat to seal completely. Serve after 3 to 4 days. If well covered with fat, this will keep in refrigerator 2 weeks or more. Allow to come to room temperature before serving."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 870.4, "protein_g": 26.7, "carbohydrates_g": 8.8, "fat_g": 79.5, "saturated_fat_g": 29.6, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 266.5, "sodium_mg": 647.0, "fiber_g": 2.5, "sugar_g": 3.0, "unsaturated_fat_g": 44.9, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["french"], "diet": [], "course": ["appetizer"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["bake", "boil", "winter"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 3.0, "count": 9}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1987-12-23", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T02:37:29.541005+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "terrine-of-pork-chez-panisse", "nyt_id": 1179, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1179-terrine-of-pork-chez-panisse", "name": "Terrine of Pork Chez Panisse", "author": "Nancy Harmon Jenkins", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "12 - 14 servings", "min": 12, "max": 14, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 60, "cook_minutes": 105, "total_minutes": 150, "raw": {"total": "2 hours 30 minutes", "prep": "1 hour", "cook": "1 hour 45 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "8 ounces fresh pork fatback", "group": null, "quantity": 8.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "fresh pork fatback", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 ½ pounds pork shoulder", "group": null, "quantity": 2.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "pork shoulder", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "7 ounces fresh pork liver, trimmed of all veins", "group": null, "quantity": 7.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "fresh pork liver", "preparation": "trimmed of all veins", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 tablespoon olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "4 shallots (4 ounces), finely diced", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "shallots (4 ounces)", "preparation": "finely diced", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 cup white bread crumbs", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "white bread crumbs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ cup dry white wine", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "dry white wine", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "4 cloves garlic (1 ounce), peeled and pounded in a mortar", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic (1 ounce)", "preparation": "peeled and pounded in a mortar", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 tablespoons chopped fresh parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped fresh parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "⅓ cup shelled pistachio nuts, parboiled 1 minute, skins removed", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "shelled pistachio nuts", "preparation": "parboiled 1 minute, skins removed", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "½ teaspoon finely ground allspice", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "finely ground allspice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "½ teaspoon finely ground bay leaf", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "finely ground bay leaf", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "½ teaspoon finely ground dried oregano", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "finely ground dried oregano", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "½ teaspoon finely ground dried thyme", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "finely ground dried thyme", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "1 ½ teaspoons black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "3 teaspoons salt", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 17, "raw": "¼ teaspoon cayenne pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "cayenne pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 18, "raw": "8 to 10 large red or green chard leaves, parboiled 2 minutes, until limp", "group": null, "quantity": 8.0, "quantity_max": 10.0, "unit": null, "item": "large red or green chard leaves", "preparation": "parboiled 2 minutes, until limp", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Slice fatback into thin strips and dice into uniform pieces, about ⅛ inch thick. Cut pork into thin strips and dice. Distribute fatback pieces on top of pork. Divide mixture in half on a chopping block and chop in two batches; chop until you have a varied forcemeat of fine and coarse bits of pork. When chopping, go over mixture with cleaver or knife several times, turning mixture with the blade, until you achieve the right consistency."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Slice liver; dice it; chop as finely as possible to a near-liquid consistency. Combine chopped meat and fat with liver in a large bowl."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Preheat oven to 325 degrees."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Heat olive oil in a small saute pan, add shallots and saute gently 5 minutes without browning until they are soft. Meanwhile, in a separate bowl, combine bread crumbs and white wine and stir until crumbs are soaked. Add wine-soaked bread crumbs, softened shallots, garlic, parsley, pistachio nuts and all spices to the pork forcemeat and mix thoroughly by hand."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Line a 1 ½-quart terrine or loaf mold with chard leaves: cover the bottom with a large leaf and overlap the other leaves around the sides, allowing them to drape over the edge about 2 inches, trimming them if necessary. Pack forcemeat mixture into mold, mounding slightly, and fold leaves over top to enclose it. Rap bottom of mold against table to settle contents and place in a baking pan with enough water to come two-thirds of the way up the sides of the mold. Bake 1 ½ to 1 ¾ hours, or until a meat thermometer, inserted only as far as the center, reads 130 degrees."}, {"position": 6, "text": "Remove from oven and let cool 20 minutes. On the terrine, place a dish or flat board and, on top of that, a weight (a 2- or 3-pound can will do). Continue cooling at room temperature several hours. When cool and quite firm, remove weight, wrap terrine well and place in refrigerator to ripen a day or longer before serving."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 391.2, "protein_g": 21.0, "carbohydrates_g": 10.5, "fat_g": 28.6, "saturated_fat_g": 9.2, "trans_fat_g": 0.1, "cholesterol_mg": 111.8, "sodium_mg": 403.5, "fiber_g": 1.6, "sugar_g": 1.8, "unsaturated_fat_g": 17.1, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["french"], "diet": [], "course": ["appetizer"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["bake", "pork shoulder", "saute", "winter"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 36}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1987-12-23", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T02:36:56.688673+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
